0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: an unchecked build checks nothing)
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build: variables start at 0, words start
0000                             ;                 undefined, and every error in the spec's table stops the
0000                             ;                 program with the four-line report, then goes to EXIT:
0000                             ;                   Err X @ line,col
0000                             ;                   <up to 16 characters of the text at the place>
0000                             ;                   Stk n: ... v v v      (n = depth, then the top 8 values)
0000                             ;                   Rtn n
0000                             ;                 S/s data stack over/underflow, R/r return stack over/
0000                             ;                 underflow, H heap, O store outside the program's space,
0000                             ;                 W bad character after [, U undefined word, Q no closing
0000                             ;                 quote, X reserved byte, Z divide by zero, N unbalanced or
0000                             ;                 mismatched brackets, B Ctrl-C.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In both builds Ctrl-C stops a running program (the unchecked build goes
0000                             ;  to EXIT without a word): see the console layer below for the rules, the
0000                             ;  held key and the break-off cell at 827Bh.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack (S); empty = 8100h. Unchecked: 127 entries.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 112 entries (S down to 8020h); the 32 bytes below
0000                             ;                 are a guard band for what a handler and an interrupt push
0000                             ;                 on top of a full stack before the check runs.
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack (U). Unchecked: 127 cells, empty = 8200h.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 126 cells (U from 81FCh, empty, down to 8100h):
0000                             ;                 the 4 bytes above are a guard band, so a handler that runs
0000                             ;                 on an empty stack writes there and not on the letter
0000                             ;                 cells. A push past the last cell lands on the return
0000                             ;                 stack's bottom entry (80FEh), and the program stops with S
0000                             ;                 before anything reads it.
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh. The break-off
0000                             ;                 cell is at +7Bh (827Bh); +7Ah is free.
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                             ; (the checked startup counts on it being
0000                             ; the page after LETPAGE)
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                COUNT:    EQU   35h   ; the break check's countdown (1 look in 256)
0000                AT:       EQU   36h   ; checked: the address of the character being
0000                             ;   run (big-endian), the place an error reports
0000                PEND:     EQU   38h   ; checked: the program's end, the first byte
0000                             ;   after its NUL (big-endian): the heap's floor
0000                SSAV:     EQU   3Ah   ; checked: S as each character starts (big-
0000                             ;   endian): the return stack an error reports
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   7Bh   ; the break-off cell (827Bh, z9+): 0 = the
0000                             ;   break key is on
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+20h   ; checked: S may go no lower between characters
0000                RSREP:    EQU   RSTOP-16   ; checked: S while the error report runs
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h-4*CHECKED   ; empty data stack (a guard if checked)
0000                DSLIM:    EQU   DSPAGE*256   ; checked: U may go no lower between characters
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Console layer: the break key. A running program reads the keyboard only
F000                             ;  through pollk and getk, which between them give the break key its rules:
F000                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program;
F000                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
F000                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
F000                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
F000                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
F000                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
F000                             ;  On a break the unchecked build ends without a word (EXIT); the checked
F000                             ;  one reports B. All three keep B, X, Y and U.
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ; pollk: the break check, at every word call and every true ")" loop-back.
F000                             ; It looks at the keyboard only once in 256 calls.
F000   0A 35        POLLK:    DEC   <COUNT   
F002   26 38                  BNE   cc9   
F004   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F007   27 33                  BEQ   cc9   ; no key
F009   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
F00B   20 0D                  BRA   ctlc   
F00D                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 with the zero flag set if there is none.
F00D   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
F00F   27 04                  BEQ   gk1   ;   the buffer (it has been through ctlc)
F011   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   
F013   4D                     TSTA      ; (CLR set Z: A is not 0)
F014   39                     RTS      
F015   BD FF 06     GK1:      JSR   KEY   
F018   27 22                  BEQ   cc9   
F01A                             ; ctlc: a key has been read. If it is Ctrl-C and the break key is on, that
F01A                             ; is the end. If the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one
F01A                             ; more key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the
F01A                             ; newest wins), and the Ctrl-C goes on: A = 3, zero flag clear.
F01A   81 03        CTLC:     CMPA   #3   
F01C   26 1E                  BNE   cc9   
F01E   0D 7B                  TST   <BRKOFF   
F020   27 1B                  BEQ   brk   
F022   34 10                  PSHS   X   
F024   8E 13 88               LDX   #250*MSLOOP   
F027   BD FF 06     CC1:      JSR   KEY   
F02A   26 06                  BNE   cc2   
F02C   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F02E   26 F7                  BNE   cc1   
F030   20 06                  BRA   cc3   
F032   81 03        CC2:      CMPA   #3   
F034   27 07                  BEQ   brk   
F036   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F038   86 03        CC3:      LDA   #3   
F03A   35 10                  PULS   X   
F03C   39           CC9:      RTS      
F03D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F03D                BRK:      EQU   fin   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
F03D                          ENDIF      
F03D                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      LDA   #"B"   ;   the checked build reports B. (The report
                              JMP   error   ;   takes S from SSAV, so the depth of the
F03D                          ENDIF      ;   calls here doesn't matter.)
F03D   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F040                             ; =============================================================================
F040                             ;  Startup
F040                             ; =============================================================================
F040   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F044   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F047   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F049   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F04B                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Zero the whole letter page: every variable starts at 0, every word
                                 ; cell at 0 (undefined: a call stops with U), and so do the
                                 ; interpreter's own cells in the gaps (KEYBUF and the rest). A is
                                 ; still LETPAGE; 256 rounds leave X at the next page, PROG.
                              CLRB      
                              TFR   D,X   
                    SZ:       CLR   ,X+   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   sz   
F04B                          ENDIF      
F04B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F04B   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ; no key held
F04D   0F 7B                  CLR   <BRKOFF   ; the break key is on
F04F   8E 83 00               LDX   #PROG   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F052                          ENDIF      
F052   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F054   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F056   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F058   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F05A   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F05C                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STX   <PEND   ; the heap may never go below this
F05C                          ENDIF      
F05C   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   
F060                             ; =============================================================================
F060                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F060                             ; 
F060                             ;    00h          end of program
F060                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh       ignored (control, space, DEL)
F060                             ;    80h-FFh      reserved: ignored, or X in the checked build
F060                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F060                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F060                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F060                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F060                             ; =============================================================================
F060                NEXT:        
F060                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler:
                                 ; the pointer minus its limit, taken as unsigned, must be no more
                                 ; than the stack's size. Below the limit (an overflow) it wraps to
                                 ; FFxxh, and the compare leaves N set; above the empty point (an
                                 ; underflow) it is just over the size, and N is clear.
                              LEAX   (0-DSLIM)&0FFFFh,U   
                              CMPX   #DSTOP-DSLIM   
                              BHI   e_ds   
                              LEAX   (0-RSLIM)&0FFFFh,S   
                              CMPX   #RSTOP-RSLIM   
                              BHI   e_rs   
                              STY   <AT   ; the place, should this character fail
                              STS   <SSAV   ; and the return stack, as it is now
F060                          ENDIF      
F060   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F062   27 D9                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F064   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F066   25 F8                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F068   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F06A   25 22                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F06C   80 0F                  SUBA   #0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
F06E   81 0A                  CMPA   #0Ah   
F070   25 2A                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F072   81 11                  CMPA   #11h   
F074   25 16                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
F076   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   ; A = c - 41h
F078   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F07A   25 2C                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F07C   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F07E   25 0A                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F080   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F082   25 1E                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F084   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F086                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F086   24 D8                  BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F088                          ENDIF      
F088                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   next   ; 7Fh (DEL): ignored
                              BHI   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
F088                          ENDIF      
F088   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F08A   80 09        P5B:      SUBA   #9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F08C   8B 05        P3A:      ADDA   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F08E                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F08E   8E F0 F4     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F091                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F091                             ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
F091                             ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
F091   E6 86                  LDB   A,X   
F093   81 14                  CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
F095   86 00                  LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
F097   49                     ROLA      
F098   AD 8B                  JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F09A                          ENDIF      
F09A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
                              JSR   [A,X]   
F09A                          ENDIF      
F09A   20 C4                  BRA   next   
F09C                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F09C   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F09E   8D 25                  BSR   rdnum   
F0A0   20 BE                  BRA   next   
F0A2                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F0A2   8D 13        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F0A4   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F0A6   20 B8                  BRA   next   
F0A8                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F0A8                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F0A8                             ; Checked: a cell still 0 (high byte 0) was never defined, since every
F0A8                             ; address in the program's space is 8200h or more. The call has not been
F0A8                             ; made yet, so the report shows the stacks as they were.
F0A8   8D 0D        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F0AA   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F0AC   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F0AE                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   e_undef   
F0AE                          ENDIF      
F0AE   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F0B0   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F0B2   BD F0 00               JSR   pollk   ; the break check, at every word call
F0B5   20 A9                  BRA   next   
F0B7                             ; =============================================================================
F0B7                             ;  Checked build: the error entries.
F0B7                             ; 
F0B7                             ;  Each entry loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside a 3-byte
F0B7                             ;  CMPX # (the 8Ch), so that a run of them falls through to one place. The
F0B7                             ;  place an error reports is the address in AT, which the inner loop sets to
F0B7                             ;  each character before it runs it; the one error that reports another
F0B7                             ;  place (W, at the character after the [) changes AT before it comes.
F0B7                             ; 
F0B7                             ;  The report counts the return stack from SSAV, which the inner loop sets
F0B7                             ;  to S before each character, so an error may come from any depth of
F0B7                             ;  calls: a handler, chkst under one, or ctlc under "?" or the break check.
F0B7                             ;  (An r sets SSAV to the empty stack.) The inner loop's own entries are
F0B7                             ;  here, where its short branches reach them; those reached from a handler
F0B7                             ;  are after h_cstore, just ahead of the report.
F0B7                             ; =============================================================================
F0B7                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from the inner loop -------------------------------------------
                                 ; The stack checks branch here with N set for an overflow (the pointer is
                                 ; below its limit) and clear for an underflow. After an underflow that stack
                                 ; counts as empty.
                    E_DS:     BMI   e_S   
                              LDU   #DSTOP   ; s
                              LDA   #"s"   
                              BRA   eall   
                    E_RS:     BMI   e_R   
                              LDX   #RSTOP   ; r
                              STX   <SSAV   
                              LDA   #"r"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_S:      LDA   #"S"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_R:      LDA   #"R"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte (80h-FFh) outside a string
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_UNDEF:   LDA   #"U"   ; a word never defined (its cell is still 0)
                    EALL:     JMP   error   
F0B7                          ENDIF      
F0B7                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F0B7   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F0B8   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F0BB   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F0BD   39                     RTS      
F0BE                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F0BE   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F0C0   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F0C2   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F0C4   39           AB9:      RTS      
F0C5                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F0C5                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F0C5                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F0C5   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F0C6   5F                     CLRB      
F0C7   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F0C9   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F0CB   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F0CD   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F0CF   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F0D1   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F0D3   58                     ASLB      
F0D4   49                     ROLA      
F0D5   58                     ASLB      
F0D6   49                     ROLA      
F0D7   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F0D9   58                     ASLB      
F0DA   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F0DB   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F0DD   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F0DF   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F0E1   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F0E3                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F0E3                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F0E3                             ; return with the carry clear.
F0E3                             ; (In the unchecked build it is here, ahead of the table, to leave room in
F0E3                             ; the two ranges after it; the checked build has it next to the grave.)
F0E3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0E3   8D D9        HEXC:     BSR   isdig   
F0E5   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F0E7   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F0E9   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F0EB   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F0ED   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F0EF   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F0F1   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F0F3   39           HV9:      RTS      
F0F4                          ENDIF      
F0F4                             ; =============================================================================
F0F4                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F0F4                             ; 
F0F4                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F0F4                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F0F4                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F0F4                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F0F4                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F0F4                             ;  stores a value.)
F0F4                             ; 
F0F4                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F0F4                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F0F4                             ; =============================================================================
F0F4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0F4                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
F0F4                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
F0F4                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
F0F4                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
F0F4                PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
F0F4                NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F0F4                          ENDIF      
F0F4                PTAB:        
F0F4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0F4   A2                     FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
F0F5   21                     FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
F0F6   B2                     FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
F0F7   8E                     FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
F0F8   7B                     FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
F0F9   D8                     FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
F0FA   87                     FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
F0FB   17                     FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
F0FC   39                     FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
F0FD   45                     FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
F0FE   E0                     FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
F0FF   31                     FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
F100   E7                     FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
F101   A9                     FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
F102   F2                     FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
F103   82                     FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
F104   8B                     FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
F105   63                     FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
F106   6F                     FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
F107   61                     FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
F108   C9                     FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
F109   C3                     FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
F10A   88                     FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
F10B   7B                     FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
F10C   77                     FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
F10D   28                     FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
F10E   46                     FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
F10F   55                     FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
F110   36                     FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
F111   20                     FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
F112   3E                     FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
F113   31                     FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F114                          ENDIF      
F114                          IF   CHECKED   
                              FDB   h_store   ; !
                              FDB   h_str   ; "
                              FDB   h_num   ; #
                              FDB   h_print   ; $
                              FDB   h_swap   ; %
                              FDB   h_and   ; &
                              FDB   h_emit   ; '
                              FDB   h_open   ; (
                              FDB   h_close   ; )
                              FDB   h_mul   ; *
                              FDB   h_add   ; +
                              FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
                              FDB   h_sub   ; -
                              FDB   h_cstore   ; .
                              FDB   h_div   ; /
                              FDB   h_dup   ; :
                              FDB   h_drop   ; ;
                              FDB   h_lt   ; <
                              FDB   h_eq   ; =
                              FDB   h_gt   ; >
                              FDB   h_key   ; ?
                              FDB   h_fetch   ; @
                              FDB   h_def   ; [
                              FDB   h_break   ; \
                              FDB   h_ret   ; ]
                              FDB   h_xor   ; ^
                              FDB   h_alloc   ; _
                              FDB   h_grave   ; `
                              FDB   h_tor   ; {
                              FDB   h_or   ; |
                              FDB   h_fromr   ; }
                              FDB   h_not   ; ~
F114                          ENDIF      
F114                PTABEND:      
F114                             ; =============================================================================
F114                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F114                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F114                             ; =============================================================================
F114   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F116   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F118   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F11A   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F11C   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F11E   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F120   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F122   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F124   39                     RTS      
F125   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F127   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F129   39                     RTS      
F12A                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F12A                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F12A   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F12C   37 06                  PULU   D   
F12E   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F130   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F132                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )
F132   35 10        H_FROMR:   PULS   X   
F134   35 06                  PULS   D   
F136   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F138   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F13A                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F13A                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F13A                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F13A                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F13A                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F13A                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F13A   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F13C   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F13E   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F140   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F142                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CMPD   <PEND   
                              LBLO   e_heap   ; below the program's end
                              CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
                              LBHS   e_heap   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
F142                          ENDIF      
F142   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F144   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F146   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F148   39                     RTS      
F149                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F149                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F149                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F149                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F149                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F149                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F149                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F149                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F149                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F149                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F149                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F149                             ; Neither the loader's stores nor the code are checked, in either build.
F149   8D 98        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F14B   24 1A                  BCC   exec   
F14D   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F14F   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F151   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F152   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F154   8D 8D                  BSR   hexc   
F156   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F158   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F15A   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F15C   8D 85                  BSR   hexc   
F15E   25 EF                  BCS   hx1   
F160   86 39        HX2:      LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F162   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F164   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F166   39                     RTS      
F167   AE C1        EXEC:     LDX   ,U++   
F169   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   ; the code's RTS returns to the dispatcher
F16B                          IF   CHECKED   
                    HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
                              BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
                              ANDA   #0DFh   
                              SUBA   #11h   
                              CMPA   #6   
                              BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
                              SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
                    HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
                    HV9:      RTS      
F16B                          ENDIF      
F16B                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F16B                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F16B                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F16B                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F16B                             ; first.
F16B                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F16B                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F16B   35 30        H_RET:    PULS   X,Y   
F16D   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F16F                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F16F                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F16F   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F171   27 40                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F173   8D 1F                  BSR   skip   
F175   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F176                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBMI   fin   ; (and FFh for the NUL: the program ends)
F176                          ENDIF      
F176   26 F3                  BNE   h_ret   
F178   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F17A   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F17C                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F17C                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F17C                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F17C                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
F17C                             ; checked build stops on it.)
F17C                          IF   CHECKED   
                    DEF1:     CMPA   #" "-"A"+256   
                              BEQ   def2   
                              LEAY   -1,Y   ; anything but a letter or a space: W. The
                              STY   <AT   ;   place is that character, just read
                              LBRA   e_brack   
F17C                          ENDIF      
F17C   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F17E   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
F180   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ;   lands 64 bytes up
F182   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F184   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F186                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F186   24 0A                  BHS   def2   ; not a letter
F188                          ENDIF      
F188                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BHS   def1   
F188                          ENDIF      
F188   BD F0 B7               JSR   cellx   
F18B   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F18D   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F18F   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F191   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F192   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F194                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F194                             ; fall into skip
F194                          ENDIF      
F194                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Checked: the skip must end at a "]" (A = 2), or for a false "(",
                                 ; which comes to opf, at a ")" (A = 0). Anything else stops with N.
                              BSR   skip   
                              SUBA   #2   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the BSR)
                    OPF:      BSR   skip   
                              TSTA      
                              LBNE   e_nest   
                              RTS      
F194                          ENDIF      
F194                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F194                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F194                             ; strings are stepped over whole. B counts the open levels.
F194                             ; Unchecked: a NUL first ends the program (for "\" with no closer; anything
F194                             ; else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets anyway).
F194                             ; Checked: a NUL, or a string that runs into it, returns A = FFh, and the
F194                             ; caller decides: "\" ends the program, "(" and "[" stop with N, as they do
F194                             ; for a closer of the other kind. The place is the opener, still in AT.
F194   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F195   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F197                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F197   10 27 FE A2            LBEQ   fin   
F19B                          ENDIF      
F19B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   ssn   ; A = FFh
F19B                          ENDIF      
F19B   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F19D   26 02                  BNE   sk2   
F19F   8D 79                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F1A1                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BCS   sk9   ; (or FFh, with the carry set: unclosed)
F1A1                          ENDIF      
F1A1   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F1A3   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F1A5   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F1A6   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F1A8   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F1AA   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F1AC   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F1AE   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F1B0   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F1B1   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F1B3   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F1B4   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F1B5   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F1B7                             ; 22h, checked build (the unchecked one is with the handlers below).
F1B7                             ; Checked: a NUL ends the string too, even right after a "/"; skipstr then
F1B7                             ; returns A = FFh with the carry set (the carry is clear at the quote), and
F1B7                             ; """ stops with Q, the string's address already pushed. (skip comes here
F1B7                             ; for its own NUL as well.)
F1B7                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
                              BSR   skipstr   
                              LBCS   e_quote   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      LDA   ,Y+   ; the character after the "/"
                              BEQ   ssn   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
                              BEQ   ssn   
                              CMPA   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMPA   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      ; the quote: C = 0
                    SSN:      SUBA   #1   ; the NUL: A = FFh, C = 1
                              RTS      
F1B7                          ENDIF      
F1B7   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F1B9   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F1BB   20 6B                  BRA   cf1   
F1BD                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F1BD                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F1BD                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F1BD                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
F1BD                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
F1BD   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F1BF   2B 17                  BMI   line   
F1C1   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F1C3   BD F0 0D     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F1C6   26 0B                  BNE   kt3   
F1C8   5A                     DECB      
F1C9   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F1CB   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F1CD   26 F2                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F1CF   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F1D1   27 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F1D3   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F1D5   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F1D7   39                     RTS      
F1D8                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
F1D8                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
F1D8                             ; is full. B = the length so far; the low byte of the top cell becomes the
F1D8                             ; most allowed (it holds minus the count on entry).
F1D8   8C FF 81     LINE:     CMPX   #-127   ; (X = TOS, minus the count)
F1DB   24 04                  BHS   ln1   
F1DD   86 81                  LDA   #-127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
F1DF   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F1E1   60 41        LN1:      NEG   1,U   
F1E3   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F1E6   5F                     CLRB      
F1E7   BD F0 0D     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F1EA   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F1EC   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F1EE   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F1F0   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F1F2   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F1F4   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F1F6   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   ; full
F1F8   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F1FA   5C                     INCB      
F1FB   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F1FE   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F200   5D           LN4:      TSTB      ; Backspace: nothing to take back?
F201   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F203   5A                     DECB      
F204   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   ; echo it
F206   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   ; A = 13
F208   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F20A   39                     RTS      
F20B                             ; =============================================================================
F20B                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F20B                             ; =============================================================================
F20B                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F20B                             ; the matching ")".
F20B   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F20D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F20D   27 85                  BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F20F                          ENDIF      
F20F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   opf   ; checked: skip, and check the closer
F20F                          ENDIF      
F20F   35 10                  PULS   X   
F211   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F213   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F215                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F215                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F215                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h. (The checked
F215                             ; build's is after skip.)
F215                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F215   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F217   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
F218   31 21        SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
F21A   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F21C   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F21E   27 F8                  BEQ   ss0   
F220   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F222   26 F6                  BNE   skipstr   
F224   39                     RTS      
F225                          ENDIF      
F225   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F227   4F                     CLRA      
F228   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F22A   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F22C   39                     RTS      
F22D                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F22D                             ; drops it and carries on.
F22D   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F22F   10 27 FF 45            LBEQ   rdrop   
F233   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F236   7E F0 00               JMP   pollk   ; the break check, at every loop-back
F239                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F239                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F239                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F239   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F23B   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F23D   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F23E   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F240   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F242   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F244   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F245   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F247   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F249   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F24B   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F24D   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F24E   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F250   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F252   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F254   39                     RTS      
F255                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F255   8D 18        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F257   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F259   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F25B   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F25C   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F25D   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F25F   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F260   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F262   39                     RTS      
F263   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F265   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F267   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F269   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F26B   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F26E   39                     RTS      
F26F                             ; ---- stack, and printing ----------------------------------------------------
F26F   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F271   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F273   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F275   39                     RTS      
F276   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F278   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F27A   39                     RTS      
F27B   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F27D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F27D   8D 4A                  BSR   putc   
F27F                          ENDIF      
F27F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   CONOUT   ; (the checked build's report is in the way)
F27F                          ENDIF      
F27F   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F281   39                     RTS      
F282                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
F282                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
F282                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
F282                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's address
F282                             ; still on the stack.
F282   AE C4        H_PRINT:   LDX   ,U   
F284   A6 80        PR0:      LDA   ,X+   
F286                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   e_quote   
F286                          ENDIF      
F286   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F288   27 F5                  BEQ   h_drop   
F28A   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F28C   26 04                  BNE   pr1   
F28E   A6 80                  LDA   ,X+   
F290   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F292                PR1:         
F292                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F292   8D 35                  BSR   putc   
F294                          ENDIF      
F294                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
F294                          ENDIF      
F294   20 EE                  BRA   pr0   
F296                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F296                             ; memory is little-endian.
F296                             ; Checked: both bytes must be in the program's space, and they are tested
F296                             ; before either is stored (chkst stops with O, the stack untouched).
F296   AE C4        H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
F298                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F298   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F29A   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F29C                          ENDIF      
F29C                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LEAX   1,X   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LDA   2,U   
                              STA   ,X   
                                 ; and fall into ".", which loads X again (and checks it again)
F29C                          ENDIF      
F29C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F29C   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDX)
F29D                          ENDIF      
F29D   AE C4        H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F29F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BSR   chkst   
F29F                          ENDIF      
F29F   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F2A1   37 06                  PULU   D   
F2A3   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F2A5   39                     RTS      
F2A6                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
                                 ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
                                 ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
                                 ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
                                 ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
                    CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
                              BLO   cs9   
                              CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
                              BHS   cs9   
                              RTS      ; in range
                    CS9:      LDA   #"O"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_BRACK:   LDA   #"W"   ; [ and a bad character (AT is set)
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; / by zero
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; _ past the limit, or below the program's end
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [: the NUL or the wrong closer
                                 ; and fall into error
                                 ; =============================================================================
                                 ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
                                 ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
                                 ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
                                 ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
                                 ;  short calls. Prints
                                 ; 
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
                                 ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
                                 ;     Rtn n CR LF
                                 ; 
                                 ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
                                 ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
                                 ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
                                 ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
                                 ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
                                 ; 
                                 ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
                                 ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
                                 ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
                                 ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
                                 ; =============================================================================
                    ERROR:    TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
                              JSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
                              TFR   B,A   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
                              SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
                              LSRA      
                              RORB      
                              LDS   #RSREP   
                              PSHU   D   ; kept on the data stack, printed last
                              JSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " @"," "+80h   
                                 ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
                                 ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
                              LDY   #0   
                              LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
                              PSHU   X   
                              LDX   #PROG-1   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
                              STX   ,U   
                    LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
                    LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   
                              LDA   ,X   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BNE   lc2   
                              STX   ,U   
                              BRA   lc1   
                    LC3:      LDD   <AT   
                              SUBD   ,U   
                              STD   ,U   ; the column
                              PSHU   Y   
                              JSR   pdec   ; the line
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ","+80h   
                              JSR   pdec   ; the column
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                                 ; the text at the place
                              LDX   <AT   
                              LDB   #16   
                    TX1:      LDA   ,X+   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #13   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              JSR   putc   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   tx1   
                    TX9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
                                 ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
                                 ; the program"s top cell, which is under the return stack"s depth,
                                 ; at 2,U.
                              LEAY   2,U   
                              PSHS   Y   ; where the walk ends
                              LDD   #DSTOP   
                              SUBD   ,S   
                              LSRA      
                              RORB      
                              PSHU   D   
                              BSR   pdec   ; the depth
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ":"+80h   
                              LEAY   16,Y   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
                              CMPY   #DSTOP   
                              BHS   sl1   
                              BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
                              FCB   " ..","."+80h   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
                    SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
                              BLS   sl9   
                              LDD   ,--Y   
                              PSHU   D   
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " "+80h   
                              BSR   h_num   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
                              BSR   pdec   ; the depth of the return stack, pushed first
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                              JMP   EXIT   
                                 ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
                                 ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
                    PMSG:     PULS   X   
                    PM1:      LDA   ,X   
                              ANDA   #7Fh   
                              BSR   putc   
                              TST   ,X+   
                              BPL   pm1   
                              JMP   ,X   
F2A6                          ENDIF      
F2A6                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F2A6   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F2A8   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F2AA   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F2AC   8D 1B                  BSR   putc   
F2AE   8D 59                  BSR   negt   
F2B0                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F2B0   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F2B3   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F2B5   8D 63                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F2B7   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F2B9   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F2BB   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F2BD   27 04                  BEQ   pd1   
F2BF   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   
F2C1   20 02                  BRA   pd2   
F2C3   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F2C5   35 02        PD2:      PULS   A   
F2C7   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F2C9   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F2CC                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F2CC   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F2CE   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F2D0   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F2D2   20 04                  BRA   st   
F2D4   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F2D6   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F2D8   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F2DA   39                     RTS      
F2DB                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F2DB   BD F0 BE     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F2DE   25 26                  BLO   negnum   
F2E0   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F2E2   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F2E4   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F2E6                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F2E6                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F2E6                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F2E6                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F2E6                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F2E6                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F2E6                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F2E6                H_DIV:       
F2E6                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDD   ,U   
                              LBEQ   e_zero   
F2E6                          ENDIF      
F2E6   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2E8   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F2EA   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F2EC   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F2EE   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2F0   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F2F2   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F2F4   8D 1E                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F2F6   8D 22                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F2F8   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2FA   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F2FC   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F2FE   8D 0B                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F300   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F302   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F304   20 03                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F306   BD F0 C5     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F309   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F30B   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F30D   40                     NEGA      
F30E   50                     NEGB      
F30F   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F311   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F313   39           NG9:      RTS      
F314   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F316   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F318   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F31A                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F31A                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F31A                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F31A                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F31A                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F31A   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F31C   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F31F   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F321   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F323   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F325   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F326   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F328   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F32B   4F                     CLRA      
F32C   5F                     CLRB      
F32D   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F32F   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F331   59                     ROLB      
F332   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F333   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F336   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F338   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F33A   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F33C   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F33E   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F340   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F342   39                     RTS      
F343                IMGEND:      


